# A command word under a home directory with a $ in it, with direxpand:
# the directory hook expands the $, rewriting the directory shorter
# than the home's expansion, and the ~ was put back by cutting the
# home's length off the rewritten match (SIGBUS). Now such a match
# keeps the rewritten directory, as bash's direxpand does. bash 5.3
# aborts here ("malloc: assertion botched"), so these screens are
# unabashed's (the vos's tests binary), not bash's.
size 10 70
rc PS1='$ '
rc mkdir d; : >d/fx; chmod +x d/fx; shopt -s direxpand
rc HOME=$PWD/d/\$NOPE
keys ~/f\t\C-a\C-kecho alive\r
